wlanpi-fpms2 (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * GPIO input hardening: request button lines per-pin so a pin held by
    another consumer (e.g. gpio-fan overlay) only disables that button
    instead of all of them
  * Retry busy pins every 30s and restart the input loop on unexpected
    errors instead of dying silently
  * Button map detection: fall back to the wlanpi-model CLI when
    /etc/wlanpi-model is missing; fix Pro match ("WLAN Pi Pro")
  * Packaging: prerm no longer stops/disables services on upgrade (only on
    removal); postinst enables and restarts services on install/upgrade —
    previously every upgrade left both services stopped and disabled

 -- Jake Snyder <jsnyder81@gmail.com>  Wed, 16 Jul 2026 04:00:00 -0600

wlanpi-fpms2 (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Align core_client with wlanpi-core pr131-packaging API
  * Hotspot endpoints moved: /system/hotspot/ssid-passphrase, /system/hotspot/clients
  * New response schemas: datetime (ISO 8601), reg-domain (country), battery
    (capacity_percent), speedtest (structured camelCase), publicip6 (info/error),
    WLAN scan (signal/primaryChannel, auto adapter selection)
  * Graceful "not yet available" pages for endpoints absent from core:
    updates, mode switch, cloud tests, profiler purge
  * Fix mode-switch action returning None on unexpected HTTP errors

 -- Jake Snyder <jsnyder81@gmail.com>  Wed, 16 Jul 2026 02:00:00 -0600

wlanpi-fpms2 (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release — decoupled state/display architecture
  * FastAPI state service with WebSocket broadcast (Phase 1)
  * wlanpi-core HMAC client with full action registry (Phase 2)
  * OLED screen thin client with PIL renderer (Phase 3)
  * Textual TUI client (Phase 5)
  * Cockpit web plugin with polling transport (Phase 6)
  * Complications API for third-party status indicators
  * Status bar indicators: battery, temperature, WiFi adapter count
  * Mode-specific home screens (classic, hotspot, server, bridge)
  * Home page QR code toggle (profiler/hotspot WiFi credentials)
  * KEY1/KEY2/KEY3 shortcut navigation
  * Profiler new-device notification popup
  * Boot splash animation and shutdown/reboot display images
  * Eth0 carrier-change screen wake
  * Display orientation persistence and flipped button remapping
  * Debian packaging with dh-virtualenv, Cockpit plugin install,
    and systemd service ordering (After/Wants wlanpi-core)
  * Conflicts with wlanpi-fpms (mutually exclusive)

 -- Jake Snyder <jsnyder81@gmail.com>  Sat, 22 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0500
